  "summary": "These <b>fragrant Vietnamese skewers</b> offer a clever one-pot adaptation of street food style minced pork skewers packed with vibrant aromatics. Juicy ground pork is seasoned with finely minced lemongrass, crushed garlic, shallots, fish sauce, and a touch of brown sugar before being molded tightly around bamboo sticks. Instead of setting up an outdoor grill, these skewers are expertly seared directly inside a <b>single heavy Dutch oven</b> on the stovetop. Searing the meat in a hot pot yields a beautifully caramelized exterior while trapping all natural juices within the pot for a quick pan glaze. A splash of coconut water drizzled along the bottom of the pot creates a light steaming effect, ensuring the interior remains extraordinarily tender while building a rich savory coating. Served alongside fresh cucumber slices, pickled carrots, and warm rice noodles, this streamlined recipe delivers authentic Southeast Asian barbecue flavor with minimal cleanup effort.",
